hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16531","He said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from men of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whom he met, mentioning that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he prevailed over Khaybar, and Khaybar became for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Muslims, and they were too weak to work it, so they handed it to the Jews to maintain it and spend upon it, on condition that they have half of what comes out of it, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided it into thirty-six shares, each share comprising one hundred shares, and he made half of all that for the Muslims, and in that half were the shares of the Muslims and the share of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with them, and he made the other half for whoever comes to him of delegations and affairs and calamities of the people."
